# TokenDamper is a TypeScript package. This file was a full GitHub Python template (245 lines,
# ~111 entries) covering Django, Flask, Scrapy, PyBuilder, Celery, SageMath, Spyder, Rope, pyenv,
# pipenv, poetry, pdm and more — none of which this repository uses, and all of which buried the
# dozen entries that do work at the bottom (audit OX-L19).
#
# Pruned to what applies. The Python block below is real: `tokendamper-benchmark/` is a Python
# harness with its own virtualenv, and `bench` shells out to an interpreter.

# Python — the benchmark harness under tokendamper-benchmark/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Node / TypeScript
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
repomix-output.xml
scratch/
.agents/
diff_report.html

# Windows Explorer per-folder settings, created on any folder given a custom icon
# or view. Never content; appears untracked in every `git status` until ignored.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
# Local MCP server declarations. `tokendamper mcp` is a shipping entry mode, so pointing an MCP
# client at this repo's own build is a useful way to exercise the adapter end-to-end — M5a, M5b
# and DECISIONS §57 were all defects that route hid from the unit suite. That config is per
# developer (it hardcodes a path into `dist/`, which a fresh clone does not have), so it stays
# out of the repo. Delete this line if a shared, committed server declaration is ever wanted.
.mcp.json
